{"id": "EUVD-2026-102479", "enisaUuid": "67ae44bc-1c1f-3aa7-b4c6-f46199f41d25", "description": "TaskingAI through 0.3.0 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows authenticated attackers to make the backend send arbitrary HTTP requests by supplying an unvalidated OpenAPI servers[0].url in a user-defined action. Attackers holding a project API key or console admin login can create an action pointing to loopback, internal or cloud metadata addresses and run it via POST /actions/{action_id}/run to read back up to 64 KiB of responses.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:08:55", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/taskingai-user-action-openapi-server-url-ssrf", "https://github.com/TaskingAI/TaskingAI/blob/v0.3.0/backend/app/services/tool/action/openapi_utils.py#L168-L169", "https://github.com/TaskingAI/TaskingAI/blob/v0.3.0/backend/app/services/tool/action/openapi_call.py#L144", "https://github.com/TaskingAI/TaskingAI", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/taskingai-through-0.3.0-ssrf-via-openapi-servers-0-url-in-actions"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111321", "GHSA-6h6x-qf3p-42m9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "41c58736-c797-3df7-a034-27393dcc7bdf", "product": {"name": "TaskingAI", "vendor": {"name": "TaskingAI"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.3.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7b4028cf-9526-3ff9-9ad8-54888ff77e86", "vendor": {"name": "TaskingAI"}}], "isExploited": false}